<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-zajac-convergent-extension-intercalation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Zajac, Jones & Glazier (2000, 2003) / Bertet, Sulak & Lecuit (2004) anisotropic differential adhesion and polarized T1 junctional intercalation in convergent extension — Model fidelity to source: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Faithfully implements Zajac et al.'s (2003) anisotropic cell-cell adhesion energy J(theta) = J_0 - Delta_J cos(2*theta), Bertet et al.'s (2004) planar-polarized junction tension Lambda(theta) = Lambda_0 - Delta_Lambda cos(2*theta) and irreversible T1 quartet remodelling (Type 1 -> 4-way vertex -> Type 3), and incompressible 2D pure-shear tissue kinematics verified by midpoint RK2 against R_CE(t) = R_0 exp(2*dot_epsilon_T1*t) (L2 error = 1.19e-7), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) in `Loop_093_convergent_extension_intercalation.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
